INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-559240cdf50d','cadw','Cadw / Welsh Government','welsh-government-and-cadw-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-3#t1','2025-11-02','Sirs/Ma''am,

I am writing regarding farmland formerly belonging to my family, which later formed part of the litigation known as BP v Buckler (1987).

I now hold a structured list of reasons and supporting evidence which I believe strongly suggest that the land transfer and subsequent development was procured by fraud and conspiracy involving government actors. The evidential threshold I now hold, if correct, would meet the reopening conditions described under s.23 of the Limitation Act 1980 – meaning that litigation, rectification and title recovery proceedings may be legitimately initiated.
','2025-11-04','Good morning,

PEDW’s role is providing an impartial appeals service, we are not the correct department to comment or provide any advice.

As there is no appeal before us, it is not in our jurisdiction.

For planning advice you can go on Planning Aid Wales website which is https://planningaidwales.org.uk/

I am sorry we cannot be of further help.

Kind regards,

Lyndsey Dennis

Swddog Gweinyddu Busnes / Business Administration Officer
Penderfyniadau Cynllunio a’r Amgylchedd / Planning & Environment Decisions Wales
