INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-036c3d02215e','hmlr','HM Land Registry','hm-land-registry-email-correspondence-catalogue#t2','2026-02-06','*Archaeological Suppression:* In 1888, my family discovered a Roman soldier in full armor beneath the living room floorboards. This discovery provided "actual notice" of the site''s national significance a century before its demolition. We allege this notice was systematically suppressed by corporate and state actors to allow for commercial development.
You''ll also see in landmark legal case BP Vs Buckler 1987 the judge says that she might have responded to BP, but to BP Pension Trust, but the claimant was BP Properties Ltd which were two separate companies. But in my dads appeal when he challenges that BP Pension Trust Ltd should have been the claimant the same judge dismissed his appeal citing both BP companies are effectively the same. This is clearly a case of heads BP won, Tails we lost.
*Missing Evidence:* Critical title deeds and Bute Estate records from our families deal with Daniel Thomas, for title after quarrying completed, in exchange for our permission to quarry, also disappeared from the loft of our home and the Cardiff Library according to my families accounts, precisely when they were needed to support our ownership claim in the Court of Appeal. Regardless we should have still remained on grounds we''d been there since 1667, and failing that on grounds of adverse possession.
It was evident lawfare to remove us, to get to the burials known about since 1888, BP profited from the land sale, the state and Crown have the exhevated artifacts and my displaced family are left traumatised, cheated and dead. My dad''s appeal was dismissed to when it shouldn''t have been and his ECHR request blocked, before dying abruptly at age just 41.

The confirmation in 1994 of a high-status Roman villa and over 1,000 burials on the exact site of our demolished home proves that the "official narrative" used to evict us was predicated on the concealment of known facts.

Under *Section 32 of the Limitation Act 1980*, the limitation period for action does not begin until such fra','2026-02-06','Enquiry Reference: 260202-5732372 Title Number: WA231076

