INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-07b00e5b9daa','cadw','Cadw / Welsh Government','welsh-government-and-cadw-email-correspondence-catalogue#t5','2026-07-15','"It is possible that the file was destroyed before it was ever updated on our electronic filing system."

These appear to be materially different positions.

Accordingly, I would be grateful if you could clarify the following:

   1.

   What evidence supported the original statement that any associated records would have been transferred to the RCAHMW or destroyed under the Public Records Act 1958?
2.

   Following the internal review, does Welsh Government now accept that there is no evidence that any relevant records were transferred to the RCAHMW?
3.

   Does Welsh Government hold any transfer lists, accession records, archive schedules or other documentation recording whether records relating to Great House Farm were ever transferred to the RCAHMW?
4.

   If no such documentation exists, on what evidential basis was the original statement regarding transfer to the RCAHMW made?
5.

   Likewise, if there is no destruction register, disposal log or audit trail relating to the relevant file, on what evidential basis has destruction been suggested?','2026-07-29','Dear Mr Buckler

Many thanks for your email, apologies for the delay in responding I have been on annual leave. To answer your queries I must refer you back to my previous emails of the 10th 3rd and 2nd July.

