INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-a8e2300f9ce2','cadw','Cadw / Welsh Government','welsh-government-and-cadw-email-correspondence-catalogue#t5','2026-07-29','However, there remain a small number of points on which I would be grateful for clarification.

   1.

   The original response of 11 June stated that associated records "would have been either transferred to the RCAHMW or destroyed under the Public Records Act 1958". As no transfer or destruction documentation has been identified, on what evidential basis was that statement made?
2.

   Does the Welsh Government now accept that it holds no documentary evidence that any records relating to Great House Farm were transferred to the RCAHMW?
Although you have confirmed wider searches were undertaken, no such records have been identified. Could you therefore confirm whether the Welsh Government''s position is that it holds no surviving correspondence, memoranda, consultation records or other documents relating to any such consultations concerning Great House Farm?
4.

   Is the Welsh Government''s position therefore that, apart from the two photographs dated 29 July 1988, no inspection report, recommendation, consultation correspondence, assessment, case file or associated documentation relating to the 1988 consideration of Great House Farm survives?','','','unanswered','unanswered','','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/welsh-government-and-cadw-email-correspondence-catalogue/#t5','cq-1881-name');
INSERT INTO qa_fts VALUES ('qa-a8e2300f9ce2','However, there remain a small number of points on which I would be grateful for clarification.

   1.

   The original response of 11 June stated that associated records "would have been either transferred to the RCAHMW or destroyed under the Public Records Act 1958". As no transfer or destruction documentation has been identified, on what evidential basis was that statement made?
2.

   Does the Welsh Government now accept that it holds no documentary evidence that any records relating to Great House Farm were transferred to the RCAHMW?
Although you have confirmed wider searches were undertaken, no such records have been identified. Could you therefore confirm whether the Welsh Government''s position is that it holds no surviving correspondence, memoranda, consultation records or other documents relating to any such consultations concerning Great House Farm?
4.

   Is the Welsh Government''s position therefore that, apart from the two photographs dated 29 July 1988, no inspection report, recommendation, consultation correspondence, assessment, case file or associated documentation relating to the 1988 consideration of Great House Farm survives?','','Cadw / Welsh Government');
