INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-90fe2855ba5e','hmlr','HM Land Registry','hm-land-registry-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-3#t1','2026-07-30','Dear Mr Haste,

Thank you for your letter of 30 July 2026 (reference N610CGV) and for identifying the surviving records held in relation to titles WA231076 and WA240304.

I am not seeking to reopen HM Land Registry’s complaints procedure or to ask for any previous decision to be reconsidered. This is a separate request for clarification arising from the additional information in your letter.

Your letter is the first to set out in detail which first-registration records survive. It therefore enables a number of factual questions that could not previously be asked with precision.

First, earlie','2026-08-12','Enquiry Reference: 260812-6561894 Title Number: WA231076

Dear Customer

I am sorry that the wrong contact information was shown on our letter to you. We are directing our customers to contact us via our contact form<https://www.gov.uk/guidance/contact-hm-land-registry#online>.

Background:

HM Land Registry has created many email addresses over the years. We can no longer service the incoming emails or route such emails into our current system.

Planned system improvements:

We plan to remove all reference to individual HM Land Registry email addresses. This process was more complex than expected and some templates still need updating.

Working with our Customers:

We want to ensure that correspondence goes direct to our customer service team. To do this, we now ask customers to use our online contact form. This is why we put an auto-response in place.','reply','thread','','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/hm-land-registry-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-3/#t1','cq-registration');
