INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-40eefa782f35','museum','Amgueddfa Cymru – Museum Wales','amgueddfa-cymru-museum-wales-email-correspondence-catalogue#t2','','Reply received: FOI - 2026-024 - Great House Farm, Llandough','2026-08-25','Dear Mr Buckler,

Thank you for your request for information received on 27 July 2026 concerning records relating to a reported discovery at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, including a soldier, horse remains and items described as a visor and lance.

Amgueddfa Cymru has undertaken searches of its collections management systems, accession records and associated documentation.

We have not identified any records relating to the acquisition, accession, donation, transfer or deposit of a medieval visor, lance, helmet or other item of armour associated with Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough. We have also not identified records relating to the specific discovery described in your request, including records of associated human or animal remains, reburial records, excavation reports, watching briefs or discovery reports.

Accordingly, under section 1(1)(a) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, our response is that Amgueddfa Cymru does not hold the requested information.

For completeness, our searches identified records relating to other archaeological finds from Church Farm, Llandough and to other archaeological discoveries recorded at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough. These records do not relate to, nor are they otherwise associated with, the discovery described in your request. We have therefore not considered them to fall within the scope of this request.

If you are dissatisfied with this response, you may request an internal review by writing to the FOI Requests mailbox within 40 working days of the date of this letter.

Cofion cynnes,

FOI Team
Amgueddfa Cymru','not-held','reply-only','','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/amgueddfa-cymru-museum-wales-email-correspondence-catalogue/#t2','cq-1881-name,cq-armour');
INSERT INTO qa_fts VALUES ('qa-40eefa782f35','Reply received: FOI - 2026-024 - Great House Farm, Llandough','Dear Mr Buckler,

Thank you for your request for information received on 27 July 2026 concerning records relating to a reported discovery at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, including a soldier, horse remains and items described as a visor and lance.

Amgueddfa Cymru has undertaken searches of its collections management systems, accession records and associated documentation.

We have not identified any records relating to the acquisition, accession, donation, transfer or deposit of a medieval visor, lance, helmet or other item of armour associated with Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough. We have also not identified records relating to the specific discovery described in your request, including records of associated human or animal remains, reburial records, excavation reports, watching briefs or discovery reports.

Accordingly, under section 1(1)(a) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, our response is that Amgueddfa Cymru does not hold the requested information.

For completeness, our searches identified records relating to other archaeological finds from Church Farm, Llandough and to other archaeological discoveries recorded at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough. These records do not relate to, nor are they otherwise associated with, the discovery described in your request. We have therefore not considered them to fall within the scope of this request.

If you are dissatisfied with this response, you may request an internal review by writing to the FOI Requests mailbox within 40 working days of the date of this letter.

Cofion cynnes,

FOI Team
Amgueddfa Cymru','Amgueddfa Cymru – Museum Wales');
INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-bf8bfecfc981','museum','Amgueddfa Cymru – Museum Wales','amgueddfa-cymru-museum-wales-email-correspondence-catalogue#t2','','Reply received: FOI Internal Review - 2026-024 - Great House Farm, Llandough','2026-09-22','Dear Mr Buckler

Thank you for your request for an internal review of Amgueddfa Cymru''s response to your Freedom of Information request concerning a reported archaeological discovery at Great House Farm, Llandough.

I have now completed my review of the handling of your request, including the searches undertaken and the concerns raised in your request for review.

Having reviewed the original request, the searches conducted and the response provided, I am satisfied that the request was handled appropriately and that reasonable and proportionate searches were undertaken in those locations where information falling within the scope of the request would reasonably be expected to be held.

In your request for review, you suggest that additional searches should have been undertaken using a wider range of terms and concepts, including references to Roman burials, military burials, cavalry burials, human remains, horse remains and other archaeological terminology. I have carefully considered this point. However, when assessing whether information is held for the purposes of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, the relevant issue is not whether every conceivable search term has been used, but whether the authority has undertaken searches that are reasonable and proportionate in the circumstances and reasonably likely to identify relevant information if held.

Your request concerned a specific reported discovery at a named location. Accordingly, the location identified in the request was used as the primary search criterion. Searches were undertaken across Amgueddfa Cymru''s information holdings where records relating to acquisitions, accessions, archaeological finds, provenance information and associated correspondence would reasonably be expected to be held. This included colle','partial','reply-only','','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/amgueddfa-cymru-museum-wales-email-correspondence-catalogue/#t2','cq-1881-name,cq-armour');
