INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-c1f0dbe4a6d6','glamarch','Glamorgan Archives','gmail:1a03f5d330ba15ad','2026-08-26','Property description – Exact wording of the land and premises. Does it expressly locate the property in Pembroke Terrace, Cardiff?','2026-09-14','‘All that piece or parcel of land with the messuage or tenement and outbuildings thereto now being erected and built or part thereof by the said lesee, situate, lying and being in Pembroke Terrace in the parish of St John the Baptist, Cardiff containing by admeasurement sixty-nine feet or thereabouts on the north side thereof, thirty-one feet or thereabouts on the east and west sides thereof and sixty-nine feet six inches or thereabouts on the south side thereof bounded on the north by land of the Marquess of Bute, on the east by Pembroke Terrace aforesaid, on the south by land demised to David Price and on the west by land of Mr John William Vachell.’','reply','item','2026/3893','https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#all/1a03f5d330ba15ad','cq-1877');
INSERT INTO qa_fts VALUES ('qa-c1f0dbe4a6d6','Property description – Exact wording of the land and premises. Does it expressly locate the property in Pembroke Terrace, Cardiff?','‘All that piece or parcel of land with the messuage or tenement and outbuildings thereto now being erected and built or part thereof by the said lesee, situate, lying and being in Pembroke Terrace in the parish of St John the Baptist, Cardiff containing by admeasurement sixty-nine feet or thereabouts on the north side thereof, thirty-one feet or thereabouts on the east and west sides thereof and sixty-nine feet six inches or thereabouts on the south side thereof bounded on the north by land of the Marquess of Bute, on the east by Pembroke Terrace aforesaid, on the south by land demised to David Price and on the west by land of Mr John William Vachell.’','Glamorgan Archives');
INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-bcef4f187c08','glamarch','Glamorgan Archives','gmail:1a03f5d330ba15ad','2026-08-26','Llandough / other references – Any mention (body text, plan, schedule, endorsements or annotations) of Llandough, Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Western Ground Rents, or any locality outside Pembroke Terrace?','2026-09-14','There is no mention of Llandough, Great House Farm or Ty Mawr or any other property outside of Pembroke Terrace.','pending','item','2026/3893','https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#all/1a03f5d330ba15ad','cq-1877,cq-1881-name,cq-1938-1939');
INSERT INTO qa_fts VALUES ('qa-bcef4f187c08','Llandough / other references – Any mention (body text, plan, schedule, endorsements or annotations) of Llandough, Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Western Ground Rents, or any locality outside Pembroke Terrace?','There is no mention of Llandough, Great House Farm or Ty Mawr or any other property outside of Pembroke Terrace.','Glamorgan Archives');
INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-14555ae14f13','glamarch','Glamorgan Archives','gmail:1a03f5d330ba15ad','2026-08-26','Marginal plan – Does the plan identify the location sufficiently?
Further identifying details – Any adjoining owners, plot numbers, parish, street numbers, measurements, previous ownership, rent, consideration, or cross-references to other instruments.

Catalogue wording discrepancy: most other 1877 entries in the series describe the grantor as the “Trustees of the Will of the late Marquess of Bute”. DBDT79/1 is catalogued simply as “from the Marquess of Bute”. From the original, please confirm who executed the lease and in what capacity.','2026-09-14','The catalogue description for DBDT/79/1 had a few small errors which have now been corrected.

1. The document is a counterpart lease dated 2 May 1877 between the Trustees of the Will of the late Marquess of Bute and Mr John Williams of Newport.

2. ‘All that piece or parcel of land with the messuage or tenement and outbuildings thereto now being erected and built or part thereof by the said lesee, situate, lying and being in Pembroke Terrace in the parish of St John the Baptist, Cardiff containing by admeasurement sixty-nine feet or thereabouts on the north side thereof, thirty-one feet or thereabouts on the east and west sides thereof and sixty-nine feet six inches or thereabouts on the south side thereof bounded on the north by land of the Marquess of Bute, on the east by Pembroke Terrace aforesaid, on the south by land demised to David Price and on the west by land of Mr John William Vachell.’

3. There is no mention of Llandough, Great House Farm or Ty Mawr or any other property outside of Pembroke Terrace.

4. The plan clearly shows a property on Pembroke Terrace. We can provide a digital copy at a charge of £15.60 (inclusive of VAT).

5. See above for full description. There is no further information included.','partial','thread','2026/3893','https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#all/1a03f5d330ba15ad','cq-1877,cq-1881-name');
INSERT INTO qa_fts VALUES ('qa-14555ae14f13','Marginal plan – Does the plan identify the location sufficiently?
Further identifying details – Any adjoining owners, plot numbers, parish, street numbers, measurements, previous ownership, rent, consideration, or cross-references to other instruments.

Catalogue wording discrepancy: most other 1877 entries in the series describe the grantor as the “Trustees of the Will of the late Marquess of Bute”. DBDT79/1 is catalogued simply as “from the Marquess of Bute”. From the original, please confirm who executed the lease and in what capacity.','The catalogue description for DBDT/79/1 had a few small errors which have now been corrected.

1. The document is a counterpart lease dated 2 May 1877 between the Trustees of the Will of the late Marquess of Bute and Mr John Williams of Newport.

2. ‘All that piece or parcel of land with the messuage or tenement and outbuildings thereto now being erected and built or part thereof by the said lesee, situate, lying and being in Pembroke Terrace in the parish of St John the Baptist, Cardiff containing by admeasurement sixty-nine feet or thereabouts on the north side thereof, thirty-one feet or thereabouts on the east and west sides thereof and sixty-nine feet six inches or thereabouts on the south side thereof bounded on the north by land of the Marquess of Bute, on the east by Pembroke Terrace aforesaid, on the south by land demised to David Price and on the west by land of Mr John William Vachell.’

3. There is no mention of Llandough, Great House Farm or Ty Mawr or any other property outside of Pembroke Terrace.

4. The plan clearly shows a property on Pembroke Terrace. We can provide a digital copy at a charge of £15.60 (inclusive of VAT).

5. See above for full description. There is no further information included.','Glamorgan Archives');
INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-b05a5736d6e7','vale','Vale of Glamorgan Council','vale-of-glamorgan-council-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-3#t3','2026-08-28','agencies holding potentially material records provide substantive
answers rather than procedural evasions;
my family is finally given a meaningful opportunity to establish,
through evidence, what actually happened.

I have no interest in mythology.

I want the documents.

I want the chronology.

I want the title deeds.

I want the correspondence.

I want the decisions.

I want to know who knew what, when they knew it, what they did with that
information, and why.

If the evidence ultimately disproves some of my suspicions, so be it.

*But the evidence must first be allowed to speak.*
And yes, I am angry

I make no apology for that.

I served this country. I spent years working in public service. I have
worked for the Vale Council. I have served in the military and operated in
circumstances considerably more dangerous than sending an email to a public
authority.

I am therefore perfectly capable of distinguishing between legitimate
administration and institutional stonewalling.

I am no longer asking to be placated.

I am asking for cooperation in recovering whatever evidence remains and
allowing it to be examined properly.

The local community members who have contacted me have long memories. Many
remain convinced that something about this episode was profoundly wrong. I
intend to establish exactly what happened — not through rumour, grievance
or inherited mythology, but through the surviving documentary record.

And if the record contradicts me, I will accept that.

But if the record supports my family, then somebody is eventually going to
have to explain why it took a descendant','','','unanswered','unanswered','','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/vale-of-glamorgan-council-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-3/#t3','');
