INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-018c3334922f','cadw','Cadw / Welsh Government','welsh-government-and-cadw-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-2#t2','','Reply received: RE: Great House Farm, Llandough','2026-09-04','Dear Mr Buckler,

Thank you for your further emails of 27, 28 and 29 August. I am sending this email as a single reply to all three of these emails.

I appreciate the importance of this issue to you and your family, and we have therefore provided all the records that we hold regarding the 1988 listing decision to assist with your research. However, we have now provided all the information that we hold, which taken together with our previous emails, I consider to be self-explanatory. There is nothing further that I can add to our previous replies, and it would be inappropriate for me to speculate on the events around the listing assessment without our own contemporary evidence being available to me to substantiate precisely what occurred. I am sorry that this final reply could not be more helpful to you.

If you remain dissatisfied with the way Cadw has dealt with this matter following this email please find a link to the WG Complaints process How to make a complaint about Welsh Government [HTML] | GOV.WALES<https://www.gov.wales/how-make-complaint-about-welsh-government-html>

Yours sincerely,

Andy Wigley

