INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-324c2cdedba3','cps','Crown Prosecution Service','crown-prosecution-service-email-correspondence-catalogue#t1','2026-09-03','Consider whether it would be prepared to take over a private prosecution under section 6(2) of the Prosecution of Offences Act 1985 if proceedings are instituted;
Confirm whether the matter should instead be referred to an investigative authority for investigation before the CPS considers taking over proceedings;
Identify the appropriate CPS division or office to which the evidence should be submitted; and
If the CPS is not prepared to consider taking over such proceedings, expressly confirm that position and the reason for it.

I am able to provide an indexed evidential bundle containing the relevant 1955 and 1974 material, historical conveyances and plans, Land Registry documentation concerning WA231076, relevant court records and a chronology identifying the specific documentary inconsistencies and matters which I consider require investigation.

I would prefer the CPS to have the opportunity to consider the matter at this stage rather than for a private prosecution to be commenced without first giving the public prosecuting authority an opportunity to determine whether it considers the case sufficiently serious, complex or otherwise appropriate for public prosecution.

Please therefore treat this correspondence as a formal request for consideration of CPS involvement and potential exercise of the DPP''s section 6(2) power, and confirm the appropriate procedure for submitting the evidence for that purpose.

There''s 133 houses approved for development on land that I believe to be concealed sacred even holy ancient welsh woodland. And my land as surviving, unestiguished claim and heir and successor of that claim has been a position our family have maintain unto our suspicious and conveniently timed deaths (my father while planning was approved for 20 houses, my nan before him in the 2 weeks she will have had to challenge BP registering and merging our land as theirs at the land','2026-09-03','Diolch am e-bostio Uned Cyswllt Dioddefwyr CPS Cymru.

Ein nod yw cydnabod eich ymholiad o fewn 3 diwrnod gwaith. Byddwn yn cysylltu â chi os bydd angen rhagor o wybodaeth arnom.

Yn y cyfamser, os hoffech gysylltu i drafod eich mater, ffoniwch ni ar 02920 803966

Sylwch, os ydych wedi cael gwybod yn flaenorol na all y CPS roi cymorth i chi ac nad yw eich ymholiad yn codi unrhyw faterion newydd, ni fyddwn yn gallu darparu unrhyw ymateb pellach.

Os nad yw''ch ymholiad yn ymwneud â''r CPS ni fyddwn yn gallu darparu ymateb, ond efallai y gallwn ddarparu manylion cyswllt ar gyfer yr asiantaeth neu''r sefydliad perthnasol.

Thank you for e-mailing CPS Cymru-Wales Victim Liaison Unit.

We aim to acknowledge your query within 3 working days. We will contact you if we require any further information.

In the meantime, if you would like to get in touch to discuss your issue please call us on 02920 803966

Please note that if you have previously been advised that the CPS cannot provide assistance to you and your query does not raise any new issues we will not be able to provide any further response.

If your enquiry does not relate to the CPS we will be unable to provide a response, but may be able to provide contact details for the relevant agency or organisation.','pending','thread','','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/crown-prosecution-service-email-correspondence-catalogue/#t1','cq-1955,cq-registration,cq-woodland');
