INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-1c8775adec45','museum','Amgueddfa Cymru – Museum Wales','amgueddfa-cymru-museum-wales-email-correspondence-catalogue#t3','2026-09-08','Any accession, register entry, day-book, donations book or correspondence in the collections of Amgueddfa Cymru or of its predecessor Cardiff Museum / Welsh Museum of Natural History / National Museum of Wales, dated 1875–1915, recording ironwork, armour, a visor, a lance, a helmet, “armour from Llandough”, or a find from Great House / Llandough Farm.

   Published sources which state that such ironwork is in the National Museum, and which therefore make a search of predecessor registers reasonable, are:

   • GGAT, Land at Great House Farm, Llandough: An Archaeological Assessment, August 1990 (planning file 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES): “it is likely that some medieval ironwork which is held by the National Museum of Wales was discovered under the rear wing c 1880 (RCAHMW 1988).”

   • Holbrook & Thomas, Medieval Archaeology 49 (2005), p. 70 n. 142: “medieval ironwork was discovered under the rear wing of Great House Farm
c. 1880. It is now in the collections of the National Museums & Galleries of Wales.”

   I note that the National Museum of Wales was not founded until 1907. If a find of c.1880 entered a public collection in Cardiff it would have done so through the earlier municipal museum. Please search those predecessor accession registers, not only the post-1907 NMW database.
Any object record for Llandough ironwork that is not labelled “visor” or “lance” but is or was associated with the farmhouse floor or rear wing / dairy (the room identified on H. J. Thomas’s 1974 RCAHMW plan).

Please treat this as a request for recorded information only.

Regards,

Sion Buckler
[redacted]','2026-09-08','Dear Mr Buckler

Thank you for your email.

I note that this request covers the same subject matter as FOI:2026-032 and extends the scope of the information requested in that case.

In order to avoid duplication and ensure that we provide a single, comprehensive response, our intention is to treat FOI:2026-036 as replacing FOI:2026-032 and to close FOI:2026-032 accordingly.

Unless we hear from you to the contrary within the next few working days, we will proceed on that basis and respond to the broader request contained in FOI:2026-036.

Please note that your request for an internal review of FOI:2026-024 remains a separate matter and will continue to be considered independently.

Cofion cynnes,

FOI Team
foi.requests @museumwales.ac.uk
amgueddfa.cymru | museum.wales

Rhif elusen | Charity number 525774','reply','thread','','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/amgueddfa-cymru-museum-wales-email-correspondence-catalogue/#t3','cq-1881-name,cq-recording,cq-armour,cq-planning');
