INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-a07f6b828faf','museum','Amgueddfa Cymru – Museum Wales','amgueddfa-cymru-museum-wales-email-correspondence-catalogue#t3','2026-09-08','FOI Team,

Thank you for your email concerning FOI:2026-036.

I do not agree that FOI:2026-032 should be closed or treated as replaced.

The three matters are distinct and should remain so.

Internal review of FOI 2026-024
This remains a review of how the original 27 July request was interpreted and searched. I confirm it is separate. Nothing in FOI:2026-036 is a comment on that review.

FOI 2026-032 (your letter of 26 August 2026; also written by you as FOI 2026-32) This is the request you yourselves extracted from my 26 August email. Its subject is the records your searches for FOI 2026-024 ','2026-09-08','Dear Mr Buckler

Thank you for your email.

I note your position and can confirm that FOI:2026-032 will remain open and will be processed separately from FOI:2026-036.

In all honesty, my suggestion that FOI:2026-036 replace FOI:2026-032 was not made with a view to aggregating the requests or considering the application of a section 12 exemption. It was intended as an administrative measure to avoid duplication of work and correspondence for a small collections team where two requests cover substantially the same subject matter.

However, I note that you wish the requests to remain separate and we will proceed on that basis.

Also, to confirm, the internal review of FOI:2026-024 will continue independently.

Cofion cynnes,

FOI Team
foi.requests @museumwales.ac.uk
amgueddfa.cymru | museum.wales

Rhif elusen | Charity number 525774','refused','thread','','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/amgueddfa-cymru-museum-wales-email-correspondence-catalogue/#t3','cq-armour');
