INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-65a2f1ce3f8c','cadw','Cadw / Welsh Government','welsh-government-and-cadw-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-2#t3','','Reply received: RE: Supplement to complaint re-served 20 September 2026 — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough','2026-09-30','Good morning Mr Buckler,

Your correspondence has been received by the Welsh Government Complaints advice team.

The complaints policy allows us to consider complaints about Welsh Government’s administrative actions (i.e. maladministration) or service failure by us. The policy is available by post on request and can also be found on our website: How to make a complaint about Welsh Government [HTML] | GOV.WALES<https://www.gov.wales/how-make-complaint-about-welsh-government-html>.

The Policy does not allow us to consider complaints about a decision which has not involved maladministration.

Your concerns will be addressed by the relevant officials within Welsh Government, who will respond to you directly and as soon as possible.

Best Regards,

Steffan Herdman
Rheolwr Cwynion / Complaints Manager
Y Tîm Cynghori ar Gwynion / Complaints Advice Team
Gweithrediadau a Chyflenwi AD / HR Operations and Delivery
Cyfarwyddiaeth Pobl a Lleoedd / People and Places Directorate
Llywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government','pending','reply-only','','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/welsh-government-and-cadw-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-2/#t3','cq-1881-name');
INSERT INTO qa_fts VALUES ('qa-65a2f1ce3f8c','Reply received: RE: Supplement to complaint re-served 20 September 2026 — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough','Good morning Mr Buckler,

Your correspondence has been received by the Welsh Government Complaints advice team.

The complaints policy allows us to consider complaints about Welsh Government’s administrative actions (i.e. maladministration) or service failure by us. The policy is available by post on request and can also be found on our website: How to make a complaint about Welsh Government [HTML] | GOV.WALES<https://www.gov.wales/how-make-complaint-about-welsh-government-html>.

The Policy does not allow us to consider complaints about a decision which has not involved maladministration.

Your concerns will be addressed by the relevant officials within Welsh Government, who will respond to you directly and as soon as possible.

Best Regards,

Steffan Herdman
Rheolwr Cwynion / Complaints Manager
Y Tîm Cynghori ar Gwynion / Complaints Advice Team
Gweithrediadau a Chyflenwi AD / HR Operations and Delivery
Cyfarwyddiaeth Pobl a Lleoedd / People and Places Directorate
Llywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government','Cadw / Welsh Government');
INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-b3eab3a31b5e','vale','Vale of Glamorgan Council','vale-of-glamorgan-council-email-correspondence-catalogue#t11','2026-09-18','The *complete County Engineer consultation response* referred to in the
report as one of the attached sheets, including the original document and
any accompanying material.

I am deliberately not relying upon the handwritten numbering of sheets ②
and ③ to identify which sheet belongs to which consultee, as the numerals
are difficult to distinguish in the surviving copy. Please identify the
corresponding sheet/document by reference to its contents or file
provenance.
Any *covering correspondence, transmission record or internal record*
showing when the NRA and County Engineer responses were received by the
Council and how those responses were placed on, incorporated into or
considered as part of the planning file.
Archaeological assessment and discharge of outline conditions

Please provide:
Any correspondence or documentation showing how the Council considered
the findings of that archaeological work in determining the subsequent
reserved matters application 92/00671/RES.
Reserved matters application 92/00671/RES

Please provide:
Any document recording the Council''s consideration of the relationship
between the reserved-matters proposal and the parameters established by the
outline permission 89/01396/OUT.
Change from the outline scheme to the reserved-matters scheme

The officer''s report for the outline application describes the indicative
scheme as *18 dwellings*, whereas the subsequent reserved-matters scheme
appears to comprise *20 dwellings*.

Please therefore provide:
Any document held by the Council recording or explaining the change from
the indicative *18-dwelling* scheme at outline stage to the *20-dwelling*
scheme submitted/approved at reserved-matters stage.
Any planning assessment, officer report, correspondence,
committee/delegated report or other record explaining the planning basis
upon which the additional two dwellings were considered acceptable under
the outline permission.
Any document identifying the relevant condition, parameter, planning
provi','2026-09-18','Dear Sion Buckler

