INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-2e81ba18c2e2','hmlr','HM Land Registry','hm-land-registry-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-3#t2','2026-09-22','Copy of register edition dated 23 February 1983
Letter from Linklaters & Paines (undated) to Land Registry

Please also send the 1971 abstract of title if it survives, whether as a separate document or as part of item 17.

I ask for the fee to be waived because:
- these documents cannot be bought on the public website for the closed title;
- you have already retrieved and, as of February 2026, scanned the historic paper files;
- I have already incurred repeated official-copy fees on the live title and related records;
- Stephen Doughty MP and the Chief Land Registrar are already seized of this file;
- the request is confined to documents you have listed as still held.

This is not a request to reopen the stage 2 complaint concluded by Mr Gill on 25 May 2026. I am not asking you to determine ownership. I am asking for copies of records you have already said exist.

If you will not waive the fee or issue the copies by email, please say so in terms, confirm that each numbered item above is still held, and state the exact OC2 wording and address so the application can go in the post without a further inventory letter.

Please reply to this email.

In light of land registry maintaining its position no mistake was made. And your confidence in the 1987 ruling. I''m trying my best to deduce if either I am mistaken or BP commited purgergy and/or concealment when registering our land parcel in their names and registering.

I''m 3 decades into my career in defence cyber and electronic warfare and I''m the son of Buckler in BP vs Buckler','2026-09-22','Enquiry Reference: 260922-6732594

Dear Customer

Please do not reply to this email. This mailbox is not monitored.

Thank you for contacting HM Land Registry. Your reference number is 260922-6732594 .

We usually reply to online enquiries within five working days but depending on the nature of your enquiry this could take up to 20 days. Please bear with us and we will respond as quickly as we can.

We will respond to Data Protection Act requests within one month and Freedom of Information Act requests within twenty working days.

In the meantime, you may find an answer to your enquiry at www.gov.uk/land-registry<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/>.

If you have used one of our email addresses we suggest using our Contact Form for any future correspondence to help us route your enquiry in the most efficient way.

The security and confidentiality of all personal data is maintained in accordance with our Personal Information Charter<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter>.

Read more about our service standards<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about-our-services#complaints>.

Peidiwch ag ateb yr ebost hwn. Nid yw’r blwch negeseuon ebost hwn yn cael ei fonitro.

Diolch am gysylltu â Chofrestrfa Tir EF. Eich rhif cyfeirnod yw 260922-6732594 .

Fel rheol, rydym yn ymateb i ymholiadau ar-lein o fewn pum niwrnod gwaith ond yn dibynnu ar natur eich ymholiad, gall gymryd hyd at 20 niwrnod. Gofynnwn ichi fod yn amyneddgar gyda ni – byddwn yn ymateb cyn gynted ag y gallwn.

Byddwn yn ymateb i geisiadau’r Ddeddf Diogelu Data o fewn mis a cheisiadau’r Ddeddf Rhyddid Gwybodaeth o fewn ugain niwrnod gwaith.

Yn y cyfamser, efallai cewch ateb i’ch ymholiad yn www.gov.uk/land-registry.cy<http://www.gov.uk/land-registry.cy>

Os ydych wedi defnyddio un o’n cyfeiriadau ebost, awgrymwn eich bod yn defnyddio’n Ffurflen Gysylltu ar gyfer unrhyw ohebiaeth yn y dyfodol i’n helpu i gyfeirio’ch ymholiad yn y ffordd fwyaf effeithlon.

Cedwir diogelwch a chyfrinachedd yr holl ddata personol yn unol â’n Siarter Gwybodaeth Bersonol<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.cy>.

Darllenwch ragor am ein safonau gwasanaeth<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about-our-services.cy> .

HM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed pro','auto','thread','','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/hm-land-registry-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-3/#t2','cq-1938-1939');
