INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-517136b677fb','heneb','Heneb / GGAT','heneb-ggat-email-correspondence-catalogue#t6','2026-09-24','Llandough Farm / Roman villa area south of St Dochdwy''s church

GGAT undertook excavation in this area in 1978–79, with the HER identifying event GGATE001109 as "Llandough Farm". The associated site record concerns an Iron Age/Roman villa complex with later early-medieval burial activity.
Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr) area north of St Dochdwy''s church

GGAT undertook an archaeological assessment/evaluation of Great House Farm in 1990, followed by the substantially larger Cotswold Archaeological Trust excavation in 1994.

These should not be conflated in the records or in any response to this request.

Part A — March 1983 warehouse fire

I have identified contemporaneous newspaper reports concerning the March 1983 fire at the GGAT Swansea warehouse.

Those reports state that substantial quantities of archaeological material were destroyed and specifically identify finds from Llandough among the losses. They also report the destruction of a photographic studio/darkroom and a substantial quantity of photographic material.

I therefore request:
Any surviving inventory, catalogue, accession register, storage list, box list, find list, archive schedule or other contemporaneous record identifying archaeological material held at the Swansea warehouse immediately before the fire.
Any surviving inventory, assessment or other record identifying material from the 1978–79 Llandough Farm excavation which was destroyed, lost, damaged or rendered unrecoverable in the fire.
Any records identifying Llandough photographic material lost in the fire, including, where recorded:

- original negatives;
- contact sheets;
- prints;
- transparencies/slides;
- photographic registers or catalogues;
- site photography logs; and
- duplicate or working copies.
Any correspondence concerning the fire or its archaeological losses with Cadw/Welsh Historic Monuments, the Welsh Office/Welsh Government, Amgueddfa Cymru/National Museum Wales, RCAHMW, local authorities, funding bodies, insurers, fire authorit','','','unanswered','unanswered','','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/heneb-ggat-email-correspondence-catalogue/#t6','cq-1881-name');
