INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-c09272ae88bb','hmlr','HM Land Registry','hm-land-registry-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-4#t1','2026-09-27','The decision came before the file was examined. HMLR gave its final decision on 25 May 2026, but did not list what the first-registration files actually contain until 30 July 2026. A final complaint decision cannot properly rest on documents that had not yet been identified.
The decision relies on a document that does not appear on the file. HMLR''s letter of 19 April 2026 described a 15-year root of title. The root relied on, a conveyance of 31 December 1969, was under 13 years old at first registration in 1982. Neither that conveyance nor the 1971 abstract said to prove it appears on the 30 July 2026 file list, and HMLR has not explained this.
The file holds examination material (form D23 and a letter of 8 April
1983) and two 1994 applications "to correct the title". HMLR has not explained any of them.
My written questions, including through my MP Stephen Doughty, have been redirected to a property search service instead of being answered.

The outcome I seek is a numbered written answer to these points, confirmation that all first-registration, amalgamation and correction records for both titles are being preserved, and acknowledgement of any failure in how the complaint was handled.

I am separately taking advice on whether to apply to alter the register. I understand that is outside your remit.

Yours faithfully,

Sion Buckler (Ret''d Sergeant)
