INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-393dc113d480','cadw','Cadw / Welsh Government','welsh-government-and-cadw-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-3#t6','2026-09-27','Sirs/ Ma''ams,

I need to correct a date I have used in earlier correspondence about Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, titles WA231076 and WA240304.

I had treated 1983 as the year the two titles were merged. That was wrong. HM Land Registry’s own letter of 23 March 2026 (Lisa Griffiths, ref N610CGV) separates the two acts. 1982–83 was first registration of two live titles, not a merger. 30 November 1982: application to first-register WA231076. The Court of Appeal later treated BP Properties Ltd as registered proprietors of “the farm” from November 1982. 23 February 1983: application to fi','2026-09-27','Diolch am eich e-bost i Lywodraeth Cymru.

  1.
Ymateb awtomatig yw hwn i ddiolch ichi am eich e-bost i Lywodraeth Cymru. Gan ein bod wedi derbyn eich gohebiaeth yn electronig, ni fydd angen ichi anfon copi papur atom.

  1.
Rydym yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn ateb yr ohebiaeth yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd hynny’n achosi oedi.

  1.
Os ydych yn ysgrifennu atom ar ran rhywun arall, gallai fod yn ofynnol o dan y ddeddfwriaeth diogelu data inni ofyn i’r unigolyn gadarnhau ei fod yn fodlon inni brosesu a storio ei ddata personol.

  1.
Ni fyddwn fel arfer yn ymateb i unigolion sy’n anfon copïau parod o ohebiaeth neu ddeisebau sy’n ymwneud ag ymgyrchoedd. Byddwn fel arfer yn anfon un ymateb at drefnwyr yr ymgyrch. Os mai wedi cael ein copïo i neges y byddwn, fel arfer bydd gohebiaeth o’r fath yn cael ei darllen a’i chadw ond ni fydd yn cael cydnabyddiaeth bellach.

  1.
Os ydym yn bwriadu ymateb, fe anfonwn gydnabyddiaeth atoch a fydd yn nodi erbyn pa ddyddiad y gallwch ddisgwyl cael ateb.

Am ragor o wybodaeth ynghylch sut rydym yn prosesu gohebiaeth i’r Gweinidogion, gweler: https://llyw.cymru/ysgrifennu-weinidogion
Thank you for your e-mail to the Welsh Government.

  1.
This is an automated response to thank you for your correspondence to the Welsh Government. As we have received your correspondence electronically, there is no need to send us a hard copy.

  1.
We welcome receiving correspondence in the Welsh language, and please be assured that such correspondence will be answered in Welsh and will not lead to a delay in responding.
  2.
If you are writing to us on behalf of someone else, then data protection legislation may require us to seek consent from them to confirm they are content for their personal data to be processed and stored by us.
  3.
We will not generally respond to individual senders of pre-generated campaign correspondence or petitions, instead we generally issue a single response to the campaign organisers only. Copy correspondence is generally read and retained but receives no further acknowledgment.
  4.
Where we will be responding, we will issue an acknowledgment giving the date by which we aim to reply.

For further information on how we process correspondence to Ministers, see here: https://gov.wales/writing-ministers

Sganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysia','auto','thread','','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/welsh-government-and-cadw-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-3/#t6','cq-1881-name,cq-registration,cq-judgment');
