INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-1c93400b1559','vale','Vale of Glamorgan Council','vale-of-glamorgan-council-email-correspondence-catalogue#t13','2026-09-28','Historic planning register
The planning-register entries that the Town and Country Planning General Development Order 1988 required the authority to keep for 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES: the applications, reserved-matters applications, plans and drawings, and relevant decision information. If the 2026 file disclosure is incomplete against that register, say what the register still lists and what is missing from the file.
Appendix B
Appendix B to the officer''s report on 89/01396/OUT: the further GGAT comments after discussions with the Trust. Case 00211463 asked for C, D and E and for a list of annexes. It did not ask for B by that description. If B is not held, say when it left the file, under what retention rule, and whether any copy survives elsewhere.
the Council''s October 1990 confirmation of condition 17;
the September 1992 reserved-matters approval, and whether any further archaeological condition was attached;
the 1993–94 papers on whether condition 18 had been discharged, including GGAT''s December 1993 letters recommending a breach-of-condition notice.
Environmental assessment / screening
Any preliminary environmental-assessment determination, screening opinion, or recorded decision that an environmental statement was or was not required for 89/01396/OUT. The application site is described as about 3.4 acres / 1.38 hectares. I am not asserting that an environmental statement was required. I am asking whether the Council made and recorded the determination at all.
Archaeological-interest consultation route
Any record of the statutory consultation route actually used because the land was recorded in the county Sites and Monuments Record, or was treated as a "site of archaeological interest" under the 1988 Order. I am not asking you to treat SMR status as automatic proof of a particular duty. I am asking what route was used.
Application receipt date
The Council''s receipt record for 89/01396/OUT. The application form is dated October 1989. The reconstructed pla','2026-09-30','Dear Sion Buckler

FREEDOM OF INFORMATION ACT 2000/ENVIRONMENTAL INFORMATION REGULATIONS 2004 - INFORMATION REQUEST

Thank you for your request for information about: Great House Farm / Church View Close — s.52/land charges, planning register, EA screening, condition 16–18 chain, 92/00671/RES

Your request was received on 28/09/2026 and is being considered under the terms of the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and the Environmental Information Regulations 2004. Your query has been given the reference 00211557.

In some circumstances a fee may be payable and if that is the case we will let you know. A fees notice will be issued to you, and you will be required to pay before we will proceed to deal with your request.

You should receive the information requested within 20 working days unless the Council does not hold the information or there is a reason for it to be withheld. We will write to you in any event.

If you have any requirements regarding the format any information should be supplied in, e.g. the language to be used, audio, large print and so on, then if you have not already done so please let us know.

If you have any queries or concerns then please do not hesitate to contact us. Please remember to quote the reference number above in any future communications.

Further information about your rights is also available from the Information
Commissioner at:

