INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-1383cac6c813','swp','South Wales Police','south-wales-police-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-3#t8','2026-09-28','Subject access, UK GDPR Article 15. Personal data you hold about me, Sion Buckler, arising from the eviction and demolition at Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, between 29 November and 6 December 1988, and from later correspondence including 719/26 and the request of 20 August 2026 concerning the deaths of William Buckler and Mary Doreen Williams. Say what identification you need before the month starts.
Crime recording. Please record, or explain in writing why you will not record, a report of suspected fraud and concealment in the creation and use of title to that land, including first registration of WA231076 (application 30 November 1982) and WA240304 (application 23 February 1983), and the 1987 proceedings. The question is whether a crime record should be opened. It is not a request that you find the civil title.
Search note on 719/26. “No records held” for a documented multi-officer operation in November–December 1988 still requires a note of systems searched, years searched, and whether South Wales Constabulary paper has gone to Glamorgan Archives. That note can sit with the internal review. I ask for it here so the crime-recording decision is not made without it.

The public evidence index is https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/ . The 1987 Court of Appeal decided possession, limitation and the October 1974 letters. It did not decide the documentary root of the farmhouse parcel. These are evidential questions. They are not a finding against any officer.

Please preserve any 1988 operational file, pocket book, custody record or transfer list. Nothing in this letter abandons any claim. This is not a claim form.

Yours faithfully,

Sion Buckler (Ret''d Sergeant)
Royal Signals
[redacted]','','','unanswered','unanswered','','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/south-wales-police-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-3/#t8','cq-1881-name,cq-registration,cq-judgment,cq-demolition,cq-1974,cq-mary-death');
