INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-7aac358661a3','cadw','Cadw / Welsh Government','welsh-government-and-cadw-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-3#t8','2026-09-30','A sentence in the middle of that letter was left unfinished. Please disregard it. Nothing in the requests depends on it.
The HM Land Registry letter forwarded by the constituency MP was dated 18 September 2026, not “yesterday”. On 27 September I wrote separately to HM Land Registry to correct a year I had used in earlier correspondence about titles WA231076 and WA240304. That correction is not a request to you.
I asked whether guidance under section 196 had been issued. Cadw’s published page now states that Historic Environment Records in Wales:
Compilation and Use (2017) is issued as statutory guidance under section 196 of the 2023 Act. What I still need is confirmation whether that 2017 text has been substantively reviewed since sections 194 to 196 came into force on 4 November 2024, and the date on which the current guidance was issued under section 196 and laid before Senedd Cymru. I would also be grateful for confirmation whether the current guidance addresses primary classification of records and the behaviour of the public interface.

What has happened since 20 September, relevant to the duties

On 27 September I made a formal complaint to Heneb concerning the HER identifiers, classification and the 1978–1995 record. Steven Foulston acknowledged it on 29 September as investigating officer, with a five-week target. That is Heneb’s own process. It does not discharge the Ministers’ duties under sections 194 and 195.

On 29 September the Royal Commission (RC26-0375) supplied the core description it says is used for GGAT02038s on Archwilio. That description is of a post-medieval farmhouse and barn. It records medieval finds, the 1974 survey and the demolition of 6 December 1988. The live HER also links the site to the separate 1994 excavation event, GGATE003875, which contains the excavation details and findings.

The adequacy question in my letter of 20 September can therefore be','2026-09-30','Neges ddwyieithog yw hon - gweler y fersiwn Saesneg isod os gwelwch yn dda/This is a bilingual message - please scroll down for English

Annwyl Sion Buckler

Nodyn cydnabod safonol yw hwn i gadarnhau bod eich gohebiaeth wedi’i dderbyn gan Lywodraeth Cymru ddyddiedig 30/09/2026, eich cyfeirnod . Ein cyfeirnod ar gyfer yr ohebiaeth hon yw TO/HF/05677/26

Rydym yn anelu at ymateb cyn pen 17 diwrnod gwaith o''r dyddiad y bydd yn cyrraedd Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae hyn yn golygu y dylech gael ymateb cyn 23/10/2026. Byddwn yn ymateb trwy e-bost ond ddim o’r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn o bosibl – felly gwiriwch eich ffolder post sothach.

Sylwer, os ydych wedi ysgrifennu at fwy nag un Gweinidog, byddwch yn derbyn un ymateb yn unig ar ran Llywodraeth Cymru. Ni fyddwch yn derbyn ymatebion ychwanegol.

Rydym yn sganio gohebiaeth bapur ac yn cadw’r copi electronig yn unig am y cyfnod a bennir yn ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd. Rydym yn cadw’r copi caled gwreiddiol o’r ohebiaeth am uchafswm o 3 mis ar ôl inni ateb. Os ydych yn dymuno i unrhyw ran o’ch gohebiaeth wreiddiol gael ei dychwelyd, rhaid ichi roi gwybod inni ar unwaith ar ôl cael yr e-bost hwn.

Os yw’r ohebiaeth yn rhan o ymgyrch wedi’i threfnu, efallai y byddwn yn ymateb i’r trefnydd yn unig, ac nid ichi yn uniongyrchol.

I gael gwybodaeth am sut y mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn prosesu gohebiaeth i’r Gweinidogion, cliciwch ar y ddolen hon: https://llyw.cymru/ysgrifennu-weinidogion

Gellir dod o hyd i hysbysiad preifatrwydd Llywodraeth Cymru yma -https://llyw.cymru/hysbysiad-preifatrwydd-llywodraeth-cymru

Os ydych am gysylltu â ni eto am unrhyw reswm, mae’r manylion cyswllt i’w cael yma: https://llyw.cymru/ysgrifennu-weinidogion

Dear Sion Buckler

This is a standard acknowledgement to confirm receipt of your correspondence to the Welsh Government dated 30/09/2026, your reference . Our reference for this correspondence is TO/HF/05677/26.

We aim to respond within 17 working days from receipt in the Welsh Government. This means you should receive a response before 23/10/2026. We will respond via e-mail, but it may not be from this e-mail address – so please ensure that you check your junk mail folder.

Please note that if you have written to more than one Minister you will receive only one response on behalf of the Welsh Government. You will not receive additional replies

We scan paper correspondence, only retaining the electronic copy for the period stated in our privacy notice. We retain original hard copies for a maximum of','redirected','thread','','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/welsh-government-and-cadw-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-3/#t8','cq-registration,cq-demolition,cq-recording');
