INSERT INTO qa VALUES ('qa-924df4ac42d6','rcahmw','Royal Commission (RCAHMW)','gmail:1a11178b91ab138c','','Reply received: RC26-0375 - Ty Mawr/ Great House, Llandough, Cardiff - Further response','2026-10-06','1) Our searches have been extensive: registered files (the only administrative records held long-term), full term-based and spatial searches of the NMRW archive catalogue, and a manual search for uncatalogued material, using all relevant site names and terms you enumerated — except the historic aerial photography collections, which would incur a charge.

2) No record of the C.N. Johns / Mrs Buckler correspondence or allusion to the same is extant in our records, with the exception of the brief note in Archive 6048945.

3) Archive 6048945 is one page, front and back. There is no surviving record giving the date or purpose of that visit beyond the description currently catalogued, nor any associated site note, field sheet, photograph, sketch or correspondence.

4) Searches of our internal records relating to these accession numbers have revealed no further information beyond the public catalogue.

5) These records have been thoroughly, physically reviewed; they relate to the sites stated in the catalogue and do not relate or allude to Great House Farm, Llandough in any way.

6) Any aerial photographs covering the site would likely be high-altitude verticals unlikely to show the site in detail. There is no further photographic record of the site in our collection.

7) The 1974 investigator''s notes by H. J. Thomas are Archive 6048943; the ink plan with additions made 12/12/1988 is Archive 6048941. We do not hold anything beyond the material already visible on Coflein.

8) [Transfers, retention, disposal] There is no record of this.

9) [Provenance of the nineteenth-century deposit account] We hold no such provenance information.

10) We do not hold any information relating to the circumstances of the December 1988 visit outside of Archive Number 6048945.

11) Physical searc','not-held','reply-only','RC26-0375','https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#all/1a11178b91ab138c','cq-1881-name,cq-recording,cq-1974');
