      - Mary Williams: Died during the precise 2-week window required to rebut the Land Registry’s registration of the land in BP’s name—a window we believe was exploited to finalize a theft.
      - William Buckler: His untimely death following the unfair dismissal of his appeal effectively blocked our path to the ECHR.

Our Position:
The Williams family has never ceased its claim. We maintain that the land was taken through criminal stealth and that the current registered titles are "poisoned" by this original fraud. We are now seeking full reparations for the loss of ancestral wealth, the destruction of the Roman archaeological site on the property, and the systematic denial of our right to a fair trial. Please provide a formal response and update regarding your position on this matter within 14 days. Regards, Sion Buckler On behalf of and one of the Heirs and Successors of Mary Williams');
