INSERT INTO messages VALUES ('m-06f14f838b51','swp','2026-05-20T08:22:00Z','received','Our Reference: LPB/26/0781','Dear Mr Buckler,

I write to acknowledge your e-mail received 14 May 2026, in reply to our e-mail of the same date.

As advised within our initial e-mail, reports and concerns regarding operational policing matters can be reported directly to South Wales Police by dialling 101 or by using their website<https://www.south-wales.police.uk/tua/tell-us-about/soh/seen-or-heard/>. You can also give crime information anonymously to Crimestoppers<https://crimestoppers-uk.org/>. The Commissioner and her team do not have access to Police systems, and it is not practice for our office to forward reporting e-mails directly to South Wales Police.

Yours sincerely,
Elinor

SWP59089
Swyddog Cymorth Sicrwydd a Chydymffurfiaeth | Assurance and Compliance Support Officer
Comisiynydd yr Heddlu a Throseddu De Cymru | South Wales Police and Crime Commissioner
Ffôn/Phone: [redacted]

Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg ac yn Saesneg.
Byddwn yn ymateb yn eich iaith o ddewis.
We welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. We will respond in your language of choice.

Ymateb nad yw''n Argyfwng\ Non-Emergency Response

Oes angen i chi siarad â''r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk<https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/>, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.

Do you need to speak to the police but don''t require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk<https://www.south-wales.police.uk/>, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.

Cymorth Iaith Gymraeg\Welsh Language Support

