INSERT INTO messages VALUES ('m-79b204087673','cadw','2026-05-20T19:26:00Z','sent','Re: Great House Farm, Llandough','I have all my evidence. Consider CADW on notice.

All I''m asking is you cooperate to find out what really happened in this case.

I''m putting together the timeline and all evidence as I believe its in the public interest and I have reason to suspect fraud.

More so I believe my family have the rightful superior claim and manorial title.

As the possible, rightful possesor of lordship of manor of Llandough, I would be the executor of the estate.

Fraud unravels all. And the limitation clock only begins from discovery not occurance of fraud. Which is this year.

So please consider yourselves, CADW, on formal notice of this concern I''m raising of fraud. Not just for reperations and narrative justice for my family, but for archelogical and historical corrections, as the gaps in records and proceedural unfairness and court mistakes and things like the ITV press coverage and 1978 news article which appear to have been supressed, all imply fraud.

In summary it looks as if we weren''t tenants but in fact held virtual freehold since 1667 and eventual fee simple absolute manorial title. Which was stolen. And thereafter my families standing was diminished and we were eventually dispossessed by armed force. Which neither estinguished our land claim nor means we surrendered, transfered, sold or gifted it. And therefore still retain claim. A reason to pursue this matter.

My family were and still are terrorised into silence and alledgedly nothing could be done about this because of the time that has past. That was until I discovered the fraud.

It would be ill advised for CADW or individuals, to participate in any past or ongoing efforts to conseal occurances of fraud.

Also consider this a freedom of information request. I require of CADW answers. Records. All you hold concerning my family and estate. Without further delay.

Regards,

Sion Buckler Esq. (Ret''d Sergeant)
Manor of Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan
bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/welsh-government-and-cadw-email-correspondence-catalogue/#t2');
