INSERT INTO messages VALUES ('m-57e09ec4787f','hmlr','2026-06-02T04:56:00Z','sent','Request for Clarification of Correspondence – Title WA231076','Sir/Ma''am,

I am writing to request clarification regarding first registration files relating to title WA231076 and WA240304.

This request is not a complaint, request for reconsideration, or application for rectification. I am seeking only clarification of the documents and records held on the first registration file(s), and the material relied upon in the registration process.

Please confirm and/or provide the following:

The full list of documents and evidence held on the first registration file(s) for WA231076 and WA240304, including the application form (FR1), transfer/conveyance deed(s), and any supporting abstract, epitome, or statement of title.

Whether any requisitions, objections, cautions, notices, or third-party claims were received or recorded during the first registration process.

Whether the file contains any correspondence, notes, or other documents of any description referring to a dispute, competing claim, or challenge concerning Mary Williams / Mary Buckler or Great House Farm / Ty Mawr.

Whether any personal documents (including but not limited to identity, marital, or probate records) relating to Mary Williams / Mary Buckler were submitted as part of the application or retained on file, and if so whether they were relied upon in the registration decision.

A schedule or index of the documentary evidence relied upon to support first registration, including any statement that copies were not retained or are no longer held.

Whether any document referred to in the registration process is noted as “copy filed”, “not retained”, or similarly annotated.

If this request is not the appropriate route for access to the above material, please advise on the correct procedure for inspection or obtaining copies of the first registration file contents.

Regards,

Sion Buckler Esq. (Ret''d Sergeant)','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/hm-land-registry-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-2/#t4');
