INSERT INTO messages VALUES ('m-0e0e57204d0c','hmlr','2026-06-03T07:39:00Z','sent','WA231076 / WA240304 – request to confirm scope of first registration file records','Sirs / Madam,

Further to my previous correspondence regarding first registration files WA231076 and WA240304, I am seeking a narrow clarification to ensure my understanding of the record set is accurate before any further request is made under statutory access routes.

I am seeking confirmation of the composition and scope of the first registration file(s), specifically what material is held, recorded, or identifiable as forming part of the application record at the time of registration.

To avoid duplication or misunderstanding, could you please confirm the following factual points only in relation to the actual file contents held by HM Land Registry:
Whether a complete first registration application file is still held for WA231076 and WA240304, including any supporting bundle of documents submitted at the time of registration.

Whether the file(s) include an index, schedule, or equivalent record identifying the documents that formed part of the application (whether retained or not retained).

Whether the file(s) contain any recorded material of any kind (including correspondence, requisitions, internal notes, or annotations) relating to any dispute, objection, or competing claim concerning the property known as Great House Farm / Ty Mawr.

Whether the file(s) contain any notation indicating that documents were “not retained”, “copy filed”, or otherwise recorded as not forming part of the permanent archive.

This request is limited strictly to confirmation of the existence and scope of records held, rather than a request for reassessment of historical matters or legal conclusions.

I would be grateful if this clarification can be provided so that any subsequent FOI or inspection request can be properly scoped to the actual records held.

Yours faithfully,

Sion Buckler Esq. (Ret’d Sergeant)
Heir & Successor to Mary Williams, Great House Farm, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan C/O [redacted], United Kingdom','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/hm-land-registry-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-2/#t4');
