INSERT INTO messages VALUES ('m-17ac09493b7c','cadw','2026-06-07T05:36:00Z','sent','Planning Permission Church View Close, Llandough','Dear Sir/Madam,

Under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and, where applicable, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004, I request copies of records relating to Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, near Cardiff.

I am specifically seeking:

   1.

   Planning applications, permissions, refusals, conditions, appeals, and related correspondence concerning the demolition of Great House Farm and subsequent residential development. 2.

   Any archaeological assessments, surveys, reports, briefs, watching briefs, excavation reports, or heritage impact assessments relating to the site. 3.

   Any correspondence between the Council, Cadw, BP Properties, BP, developers, archaeologists, the Royal Commission, or other public bodies concerning:
   - Great House Farm;
      - its historic significance;
      - archaeological discoveries;
      - listing or scheduling considerations;
      - demolition proposals.
   4.

   Any records discussing reported Roman remains, medieval remains, monastic remains, burials, architectural fragments, or other archaeological features associated with the site. 5.

   Any records relating to emergency listing, spot-listing, preservation, or protection measures considered for Great House Farm during the 1980s. 6.

   Any committee minutes, officer reports, recommendations, or briefing papers relating to planning decisions affecting the site.

If some records are held in archives or under a different authority, please advise where they may be located.

I would prefer the information in electronic format.

Yours faithfully,

Sion Buckler

https://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz','https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/records-access-chronology/foi-reply-register/welsh-government-and-cadw-email-correspondence-catalogue-part-3/#t5');
