INSERT INTO messages VALUES ('m-a938df7cba32','swp','2026-06-07T08:25:00Z','sent','FOI/EIR Request – 1988 Police/Bailiff Involvement in Dispossession at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough (Ref: Buckler/Williams Family, BP Properties)','FOI Team / South Wales Police,

I am Sion Buckler (heir/successor of Mary Williams, d. 1983), writing
formally under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and Data Protection
legislation regarding the 1988 dispossession/eviction at Great House Farm
(Ty Mawr / Church View Close area), Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan.

Please provide all held records, correspondence, incident logs, statements,
photographs, or reports from 1900-1993 concerning:
- Police attendance/support for bailiffs at the property (including
chainsaw incident, barricading, sledgehammers).
- Any involvement with BP Properties, Western Ground Rents, or Bute Estate
successors.
- Mentions of Williams/Buckler family occupancy, Mary Williams'' prior
claims, quarry deal with Daniel Thomas, house ownership vs. leased farmland.
- Any complaints, use of force, or outcomes.
- Any association/ collaboration with military forces, officers, defence
staff/ personnel regarding my families eviction in 1988

Here''s a YouTube on what I theorise on what happened at the address
https://youtu.be/INfFOLndny0?feature=shared

I request a litigation hold on all related files. Full details available on
request.

Thank you,

Sion Buckler
