INSERT INTO messages VALUES ('g-1a03f6bf8659fbd6','glamarch','2026-08-26T18:53:54Z','sent','DBDT79/1 – physical examination of the original','Request: physical examination of DBDT79/1. Catalogue entry: Lease (counterpart) of land and premises situate in Pembroke Terrace, Cardiff, from the Marquess of Bute to Mr John Williams, May 1877 [1 parchment, plan in margin].

1. Parties and date – Does the original name the Marquess of Bute and Mr John Williams, and is it dated May 1877?

2. Property description – Exact wording of the land and premises. Does it expressly locate the property in Pembroke Terrace, Cardiff?

3. Llandough / other references – Any mention (body text, plan, schedule, endorsements or annotations) of Llandough, Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Western Ground Rents, or any locality outside Pembroke Terrace?

4. Marginal plan – Does the plan identify the location sufficiently?

5. Further identifying details – Any adjoining owners, plot numbers, parish, street numbers, measurements, previous ownership, rent, consideration, or cross-references to other instruments.

Catalogue wording discrepancy: most other 1877 entries in the series describe the grantor as the “Trustees of the Will of the late Marquess of Bute”. DBDT79/1 is catalogued simply as “from the Marquess of Bute”. From the original, please confirm who executed the lease and in what capacity.','https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#all/1a03f5d330ba15ad');
INSERT INTO messages_fts VALUES ('g-1a03f6bf8659fbd6','DBDT79/1 – physical examination of the original','Request: physical examination of DBDT79/1. Catalogue entry: Lease (counterpart) of land and premises situate in Pembroke Terrace, Cardiff, from the Marquess of Bute to Mr John Williams, May 1877 [1 parchment, plan in margin].

